2 Ali  2000
3 John NULL
```

***

# ✅ 4. Join on Different Column Names

```python
df1.join(df2, df1.id == df2.emp_id, "inner").show()
```

***

# ✅ 5. Multiple Conditions

```python
df1.join(df2, (df1.id == df2.id) & (df1.name == df2.name), "inner").show()
```

***

# ✅ 6. Handling Duplicate Columns

```python
df1.join(df2, "id").select(df1["id"], df1["name"], df2["salary"]).show()
```

***

# 🔥 Quick Summary

| Join Type | Description                      |
| --------- | -------------------------------- |
| Inner     | Only matching rows               |
| Left      | All left + matched right         |
| Right     | All right + matched left         |
| Outer     | All rows from both               |
| Left Semi | Only matching rows from left     |
| Left Anti | Only non-matching rows from left |

* Default join = **Inner join**
